---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Async IO"
  description="What async-io.live collects, who processes it, and how to reach Async IO about your personal information."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="legal">
    <article class="legal-container">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <span class="section-label">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-lede">
          Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time>.
          This policy covers async-io.live, including the documentation at
          <a href="/docs/">async-io.live/docs/</a>. It describes what is collected
          when you visit, who processes it, and how to reach us.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>This site sets no cookies of its own and runs no advertising or cross-site tracking.</li>
          <li>Visit statistics are aggregate and cookieless.</li>
          <li>We only hold personal information you choose to send us: an email, or a call you book.</li>
          <li>We do not sell or rent personal information.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Visit statistics</h2>
        <p>
          We count visits with <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible Analytics</a>,
          which works without cookies. It records aggregate figures (pages viewed, referring site,
          browser, operating system, device type and country) that do not identify you,
          and we use them only to see which pages are read.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by GitHub Pages. GitHub logs the IP address of visitors for security
          purposes, as described in the
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
          Fonts and scripts on this site are served from async-io.live, except the analytics
          script above and the scheduling widget below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Booking a call</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> embeds a
          <a href="https://calendly.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Calendly</a>
          scheduler. Calendly loads only on that page. If you book, Calendly collects the name,
          email address and answers you enter, and may set its own cookies. We receive the booking
          and use it to prepare and hold the call.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          When you write to <a href="mailto:support@async-io.org">support@async-io.org</a>, we use your
          message and address to answer you and, if you are a customer, to provide the support you
          pay for. We keep that correspondence for as long as the conversation or the support
          relationship needs it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, have it corrected or
          deleted, or withdraw a consent you gave. Write to
          <a href="mailto:support@async-io.org">support@async-io.org</a>, which reaches the person
          in charge of the protection of personal information at Async IO. We answer within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Async IO is based in Quebec. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can contact the
          <a href="https://www.cai.gouv.qc.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec</a>,
          or the data protection authority where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: calc(var(--space-4xl) + 60px) var(--space-xl) var(--space-4xl);
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .section-label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-lede {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .legal section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .legal p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal {
      padding: calc(var(--space-3xl) + 60px) var(--space-md) var(--space-3xl);
    }
  }
</style>
